      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Metastases from cutaneous basal cell carcinomata are extremely rare phenomena. The majority of haematogenous metastases occur (in descending order) in the lung, skin and liver. The ratio of lymphogenic to haematogenic metastases is approximately 1 to 1. An exceedingly rare case of a metastasis to skeletal muscle is presented."},
